The '''Nevarro Mandalorian covert'''<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: Character Encyclopedia, Updated and Expanded Edition]]''</ref> was a [[Mandalorian]] [[covert]] hidden in the [[Nevarro sewer|sewers]] of [[Nevarro]] by the [[New Republic Era|time]] of the [[New Republic]]. The covert was operated by [[the Tribe]]. It was a place where Mandalorians could remain in secret, and preserve their creed and way of life.<ref name="The Star Wars Book">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref> According to [[Paz Vizsla]], [[the Tribe]] were only allowed out of the enclave one at a time.<ref name="Chapter 3" />

The covert was the home of Mandalorian [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] after the fall of the [[Galactic Empire]]. He visited an [[The Armorer|armorer]] there, who made him a [[pauldron]] and later a full cuirass from [[beskar]] steel he provided.<ref name="Chapter 1" /><ref name="Chapter 3">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref> The covert was left abandoned following the [[Attack on the Tribe|massacre]] of the Tribe members.<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref> The Armorer and Vizsla, who survived the attack, later established a new [[Mandalorian covert|covert]] on the [[space station]] [[Glavis Ringworld]].<ref name="BoBF Chapter 5">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref>

